+# Runtime hardening & sandboxing runbook (summary)
+
+Overview
+- Run untrusted or user-facing workloads in isolated runtimes (runsc / microVM) and enforce seccomp & non-root containers.
+- Use RuntimeClass with runsc or Kata where supported. For highest isolation, use Firecracker / Ignite microVMs in a dedicated operator pattern.
+
+Steps
+1. Configure RuntimeClass and ensure node containerd supports runsc / kata.
+2. Apply seccomp profile (deploy/k8s/seccomp/secure_worker_seccomp.json) to worker pods via annotation or Pod spec.
+3. Use runtimeClassName: runsc in Pod specs for high-risk workloads (see deploy/k8s/secure_worker_pod.yaml).
+4. For microVM-level isolation, evaluate Ignite / Firecracker operator and deploy workers into microVM pool.
+5. Restrict network egress with NetworkPolicy and deny by default for sandbox pods; allow only audit/evidence endpoints.
+6. Enforce image allowlist and cosign-signed images before admission via admission controller.
+7. Monitor worker pods for unexpected syscalls, cgroup anomalies, and high execve counts.
+
+Notes
+- MicroVM orchestration and operator installation is vendor-specific. Treat this runbook as a starting checklist and engage platform SRE to implement per-cluster.
